1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,330
The baker Elias sat by his cooling loaves, the scent of yeast and cinnamon heavy in the

2
00:00:05,330 --> 00:00:06,040
evening air.

3
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:09,080
His hands dusted with flour trembled.

4
00:00:09,670 --> 00:00:12,480
The harvest had been poor and his larder was nearly bare.

5
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:15,590
Fear, cold and sharp had settled in his chest.

6
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:20,850
His neighbor, Old Martha, had a small patch of ripe tomatoes, but Elias couldn't bring

7
00:00:20,850 --> 00:00:24,960
himself to ask, pride like a stubborn stone blocked his throat.

8
00:00:26,050 --> 00:00:29,550
A gentle voice like the rustle of wheat broke his reverie.

9
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:32,890
A heavy heart makes for stale bread, my friend.

10
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:34,250
Elias looked up.

11
00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:39,890
A man stood there, his eyes as warm as the oven's glow, a faint smile playing on his lips.

12
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:42,100
He wore simple, travel -worn clothes.

13
00:00:43,020 --> 00:00:45,960
The harvest, Elias mumbled, gesturing vaguely.

14
00:00:46,340 --> 00:00:48,530
It is difficult, the man nodded.

15
00:00:49,020 --> 00:00:54,140
Indeed, but sometimes the smallest seed shared can grow into the most bountiful harvest.

16
00:00:55,460 --> 00:01:00,740
He reached into a worn satchel and pulled out a single, perfect apple, its skin a blushing

17
00:01:00,740 --> 00:01:01,320
crimson.

18
00:01:02,170 --> 00:01:06,930
I have only this, but it is yours, Elias blinked, surprised, but you need it.

19
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:12,790
We all need something, the man replied, his gaze steady and kind, but sometimes giving

20
00:01:12,790 --> 00:01:15,150
what little we have is the greatest way to receive.

21
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:18,700
He placed the apple in Elias' trembling hand.

22
00:01:19,790 --> 00:01:25,590
Think of it this way, a hand that hordes a single apple will never know the joy of sharing a basket.

23
00:01:26,780 --> 00:01:32,850
Elias watched the man walk away, a warmth spreading through him that had nothing to do with the fading sun.

24
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:38,620
He looked at the apple, then at Martha's small garden, now bathed in the soft twilight.

25
00:01:39,210 --> 00:01:43,070
He stood, the apple clutched in his hand and walked towards her door.

26
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:47,180
The smallest act of generosity can nourish the deepest hunger.

